WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.367
-Alright, thank you so much.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.968
I got five seconds.
Thank you.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.901
[ Laughter ]
Wow, man, this is great.
This is so cool.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.501
I'm on "The Tonight Show
with Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:09.734
This is so cool.
This is my first late night,

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.601
you know, thing
and I'm really excited for it

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.267
because I hope people
recognize me.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.901
[ Cheering and applause ]
I like that, man.
That's cool.

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:19.100
I just, you know, I love --
I love when people recognize.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.601
People think they're bothering
me when they recognize me.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:23.100
They're like, "Hey, Preacher,
I don't mean to bother you,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.501
but can I get a picture?"
Then I got to play it off

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.400
like I don't need it
for my self-esteem, right?

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.367
[ Laughter ]
"Alright, fine. I got you."

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:32.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:33.467
That's what I do on the outside.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.634
On the inside, I'm like,
"Oh, my God!"

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
I love it.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.467
I just, I hate when people

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.100
recognize me
and say weird things.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.868
Like some people come up to me,
they're like,

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.267
"You look big on TV."

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.667
[ Laughter ]
Okay.

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:45.901
You got a big TV, then.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:48.868
I don't know what to tell you.
I'm sorry you

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.033
catfished yourself, bruh.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.868
[ Laughter ]
Like I'm not even short.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.501
I'm 5'11", right?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:55.434
Like actually.
Like I'm not Tinder 5'11"

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:57.100
and you meet me in person,
I'm like, "Hey, baby,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.434
how you doing, girl?
Hey.

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.100
[ Laughter and applause ]
Let me get that door for you.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:00.868
Let me get that, you know."

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:02.501
[ Laughter ]
You know?

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:04.133
It says I'm 5'9" online.

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:06.767
I Googled me.
It said I'm 5'9", right?

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.467
No, I'm not, bro, okay?
I'm a man. I need my inches.

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:12.067
So I talked to my manager.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.367
I was like,
"Yo, bro, you got to fix that."

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.567
He's like,
"I wouldn't worry about that."

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.400
Of course you wouldn't,
you 6'2" idiot.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.834
You already made it, okay?

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.534
I don't know who did that,
but when I see you, bro,

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:21.934
I'mma high-five your face, bro.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.334
I swear to pop.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:26.133
Alright? I've been
training some MMA, you know?

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.868
I've been doing UFC.
See some people call it UFC.

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.000
"You do UFC?"

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.267
Like, UFC is the organization.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:33.334
MMA, mixed martial arts,
is the sport.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:36.968
That's like saying, "You do NBA?
You do Golden State Warrior?"

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.934
It's basketball, you know?

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:41.634
So, I've been training
a few years.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.467
I started training
on my ex-girlfriend's birthday

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.367
because I was like,
"Wow, I really miss her."

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:46.534
And I was like,
"What if she has a boyfriend?"

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:47.734
And that's all I needed.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:50.033
So I was like,
"Time to learn how to fight."

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:53.200
So I went to this
MMA gym called Uprise in L.A.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.200
It was great.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.000
I start hitting,
like, heavy bags.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.501
I was doing,
like, mitts and stuff.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:58.701
And then my coach, Pete --
he was like,

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.868
"Hey, man, you move
around pretty good.

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.834
Why don't you come to one
of these sparring sessions,

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.167
do some light fighting?"

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.901
And I was like, "Well, I'll do
some light fighting, bro.

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:08.100
All you do is twist, right?
I got it, man."

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.567
So I went to a sparing session
and I brought a Tinder date

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:12.667
to the sparring session.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.100
And -- Yeah, I know now.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:19.300
And the first person I sparred,
he was like 6'19".

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.801
[ Laughter ]
He was three people
bigger than me.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.834
He had tattoos.
I don't know if y'all know this,

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.667
but tattoos make you stronger.

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:27.100
[ Laughter ]
And...

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.133
I didn't realize he used
to date the girl

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.367
that I brought
on the Tinder date.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:34.634
They were engaged.
They had children together.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.334
I don't know
if any of that's true,

00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:38.400
but he was hitting me
like that, okay?

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.567
[ Laughing ]

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:41.234
This man kicked me.

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:43.767
He kicked me in the stomach
so hard, I hit the Kaepernick.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.400
I was like,
"Ooh, Black Lives Matter.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.767
You don't understand
what we go through."

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:51.200
[ Applause ]

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.367
He was Black, too.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:56.200
I was like, "You gonna do
your brother like this?"

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.100
So, but I kept training,
I kept training,

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.200
and I feel good.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.267
And so I was like,
you know what?

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.501
I'm gonna do an actual
MMA match, right?

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:05.300
So I did my first one
in January,

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.334
so that was pretty cool.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.767
People are like, "That's
weird that you do MMA.

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:09.934
You don't seem violent."

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:11.267
And I'm not. Like,
I'm ticklish, you know?

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:14.434
Like, if I'm ever choking you,
goochie goochie goo.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:17.067
You out. I got to let you go.
I can't, you know?

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.734
I listen to R&amp;B music when
I'm working out, you know?

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:22.434
My walk-out song to my match

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.334
was "Strawberry Kisses"
by Amber-Simone.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:25.934
You know what I mean?

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:28.601
And my opponent, he came out to
"I'mma kill you, die" music.

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.200
Like, I don't even
remember the song,

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.467
but I remember walking out
and I was like,

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:33.968
I was having a lot of fun.

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:36.667
I was like, I was loose and
I wasn't nervous at all, man.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:38.667
My friends and family members
were there and I was like,

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.167
It's going to be great.

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:41.567
And I looked across the cage
and I see him and I'm like,

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.834
"Wow, he look...
he way bigger than I remember."

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.901
And I was like,
"Is that a tattoo?"

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:50.400
And then the bell rang
and we came out and I was like,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.734
"Let's go," and I hit him with,
like, three punches.

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:52.767
I was like, pop, pop, pop.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:53.968
And I was like, oh, snap.

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:56.000
Maybe I'm a bad person,
because I liked it.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.000
So I threw a bunch of punches,
but I forgot to breathe.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.667
When you watching fighters,
they breathe.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:01.868
Ha-ha-ha!

00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:03.200
And I was like --

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:06.033
[ Laughing ]

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.400
Right? Right?

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:12.901
So imagine swinging
as hard as you can underwater.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.367
And then as soon
as you get above water,

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:15.934
someone tackles you,
'cause that's what he did.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.100
I was down! He's tackling me!

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.601
Is he on my back?
Is he choking me?

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.133
[ Strained ]
Yep! He choking me.

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:23.467
And I look across the cage
and I see my brother.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.868
He goes, "Ehh," and I'm like...

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:26.901
What does that mean?

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:28.033
My friend was recording.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.601
He's like,
slowly putting his phone down.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:32.167
Like, "I don't know this dude."

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:33.701
I hear my mom yell out,

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.934
"Get off my baby!"

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:41.367
[ Applause ]

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:43.734
I was like, I think I'm losing
right now.

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.167
My name is Preacher Lawson.
Thank you so much.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:46.801
I love you. Thank you.

